# Continue the equilibrated TIP4P/2005 slab and write one oxygen frame
# every `stride` steps. `ntrans` transitions need stride*ntrans steps
# after the frame at step 0, which is the equilibrated configuration.
# Thermostat, barostat and step are those of in.tip4p.equilibrate.
# The restart carries positions, velocities and the box. The pair style,
# Shake and the barostat are stated again because a restart does not
# keep them. Only oxygens are written: the neighbour graphs are
# oxygen-only.

variable stride index 5
variable ntrans index 200
variable temp index 252.0

units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p
atom_modify map array

read_restart equil.restart
# The restart restores the long-range pair style, which will not
# initialise until the kspace style is set.
kspace_style pppm/tip4p 1.0e-4
pair_style lj/cut/tip4p/long 1 2 1 1 0.1546 10.0
pair_modify mix arithmetic
pair_coeff 1 1 0.1852 3.1589
pair_coeff 2 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff 1 2 0.0 1.0

bond_style harmonic
bond_coeff 1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style harmonic
angle_coeff 1 55.0 104.52
special_bonds lj/coul 0.0 0.0 0.0
reset_atoms image all

neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix shake all shake 0.0001 20 0 b 1 a 1
fix bath all npt temp ${temp} ${temp} 200.0 z 1.0 1.0 2000.0

timestep 2.0
thermo 5000
thermo_style custom step temp pe press density

reset_timestep 0
group oxygen type 1
variable nsteps equal ${stride}*${ntrans}
dump 1 oxygen custom ${stride} prod.lammpstrj id type x y z
dump_modify 1 sort id
run ${nsteps}
